The startscum:
My initial games were startscums to try to get either a
blindfold/towel in starting room, or a blessed smoky potion (healers
start with healing and extra healing) or a starting room fountain
wish. After a while, though, I realized this was non intentionally
scumming for games with an identified and common smoky potion type, so
I stopped doing it. As for the fountain wish, when I got one I asked
for a cursed blindfold so as not to remove it accidentally, and so
that
monkeys could not steal it (these advantages are somewhat paid for
with increased prayer timeout). However, the ascending game started
with randomly generated blindfold.
The Constitution value was the second most important thing I looked at
the start (max HP is very important), but I was not scumming for that.

Total number of games: 3178
Number of games with starting blindfold/towel/wish : 18
Ascension ratio ~ 5.5%
For comparison, my zen ascension ratios are (sam,100%), (mon,100%),
(pri,100%), (wiz,20%), (rog,8.3%), (tou,0.3%), even if priests and
monks ratios are misleading (I have confidence in my samurais).

Before I go into the details of the actual ascension, though, I want
to rant a bit about my failures.
The very first game I started with a blindfold was very promising and
very good. I started with 18 constitution, survived an early epic
battle with a werejackal and its brethren, I received an early
magicbane (4k turns) and generally the game went pretty good. I even
completed the quest, but when I cleared the castle, instead of
regrouping (wishing, identifying, enchanting, etc) I decided to go
clear the VoD and died to a small L summon storm. My excuse is that I
had not been playing recently and had lost the feeling to the dangers.
A little less stupid me would have easily ascended this game and
obtained an artificial 100% ascension rate.
Another YASD was at the bigroom. I don't know how, but I managed to
get cocky. Even in regular games I strongly defend the upstairs, but I
decided to go eat some giant I had just killed. A lizard occupying the
upstairs, some heavy hits and failed Elbereths did the rest. It would
not be a garanteed ascension, but I was doing pretty good (mjollnir
and magicbane).
Yet another frustrating failed game: while I am recovering from stun
(stalker corpse), a nymph is generated and approaches me. I couldn't
hit her or run away because I could hit a peaceful monkey and create
another robber, so I stood still while she took my magicbane, of all
my items. Fine, I decided to go tame a pet to kill her, but it hits a
levelport trap. At this point I had to wield something, so I had
chosen a stack of 5 daggers, which where cursed. While dipping in
fountain for remove curse, I got water mocassins, which ended the
game.
The last frustrating game qualifies more for a YAAD than a YASD, since
the floating eyes (there were 9 in total) did not leave corpses. While
in DLV 1, I had two monkeys steal my scalpel (but not my blindfold,
due to cursed status), but I successfully hunted them down and
retrieved my gear. However, by turn 15K a nymph appears, and I had to
go camp on DLV 2. After around more 2K turns I finally died.

One idea (probably nothing new to most of you) it occurred to me in
these games, which I did not do in my actual ascension since I got
magicbane rather lately: to go kill nymphs, surround every square
around it with an item-protected Elbereth.

The ascension:
Started with randomly generated blindfold. Started with only 13 Con,
but with quaffed potions and a bit of luck I got decent hit points.
There was an altar on level 1, but before I could camp there I had to
raise some levels, so I explored a couple of Dlvs below. At some point
I found a werejackal at DLv2 (stethoscope is a very powerful tool for
a zen character). I've had many troubles with werefoo in my zen
healers, specially because they start with no armor (MC0) and have low
damage hits, so I decided to camp on DLv1 until I got an artifact
weapon. At the precise moment I climbed the stairs it was right next
to me, so I don't know why it didn't follow. Maybe it was on jackal
form? In any case, that provided some precious time.
Eventually I got a floating eye corpse and a gift: Cleaver, while I
really wanted Magicbane for the engraving. I decided to camp a bit
more just to remove the prayer timeout, and a wererat gives me
lycantropy before I can kill it. So, more time on DLv1 just to cure
that, and there are corpses you can't carry while in rat form.
Next I went for the mines, and as soon as I got a dwarvish cloak I put
it on. Minetown was a bit of a let down: altar was cross aligned and
there was no general shop. Actually, there was no general shop in the
entire dungeon, which would be very bad for a zen game, but there are
tricks to circumvent this: put the items you want to identify inside a
container, drop it on the entrance of the shop and make your pet carry
it inside (basically, reverse shoplifting). Then, after some credit
cloning buy back the items the shopkeeper would not usually trade with
you. As for really identifying the items (as oposed to 'see' them) you
have to use the buying prices. Since I never got the hang of those, I
only got an idea of the range of the base prices. At least there was a
bookstore, which I used to price-id the scrolls. Also, from the upper
mines levels I got some armor (BUC-tested with pet), including a +1
dwarvish mithril.

Back on the main dungeon, the first blunder of the game: while
'T'aking off armor to cast StF on a boulder, I accidentally pressed R
and removed the blindfold. I was on a corridor, so I didn't get new
information, and after considering quiting for the first time I Put
the blindfold back on and resumed the game.
On the very next level, a nymph (apparently generated next to me while
I was eating) stole my Cleaver. I was still angry at the previous
mistake, and this inconvenience almost made me quit. Only the
startscuming bother made me continue, and I returned to DLv1 to get
another gift, this time Frost Brand.
Hunting the nymph both of us fall through a trap door, so I can't go
back up. Exploring the level, I hit a sleep trap (twice, the second
time was sheer stupidity) and the n steals Frost brand. After a while
and some dangerous turns wielding the scalpel the n hit the sleep
trap, so I killed her and retrieved my stuff.

At turn ~22K, DLv8 I got a throne wish : +2SDSM, and luckily sokoban
had a BoH. After some more exploration I returned to the mines to
price-id scrolls, get the luckstone and reverse-shoplift-id my
potions.

At turn ~59K, Dlv17 I had a risky encounter with a golden Naga, but I
only lost my boots. At Dlv20 there was a demi-lich, so I returned to
my stash to have my first id-session: quaffed a B!ObjDet, zap-id most
wands and pet-tested BUCs. Then I went to pray for holy water, and
with a bit of saccing and luck got Magicbane. After blessing some ?oId
my first one identified all inventory: luckily one of the scrolls was
genocide, and one of the rings was teleport control. I also had two
magic markers, so I genocided L, h (disenchanters a bit later, golden
nagas and ; a lot later). Much later I would also successfully
reverse-genocide tengu for TC.
At this point I was able to and did the quest, so now I also had the
staff of aesculapius.

At Dlv26, just above Medusa, I got 2 wishes from a throne: +2[MR and
+2[HoT (just for the astral plane). I still didn't have a reliable
method for crossing Medusa level (titan version), so I dug down and
got [oL from Perseus.
At around turn 88K I started exploring Gehennom. Although I spent a
lot of time there, since I explored it the hard way (I live for the
loot), it was mostly uneventful. After detecting the VS I did my final
preparations, including alchemy ( 183 HP -> 375 ), being crowned (so
that vorpal blade was not generated on astral) and genociding nymphs
just for revenge of previous games.

The ascension run:
While performing the invocation I made my second blunder. I don't know
what I applied instead of the bell, but when I removed the blindfold
to read the +oD, I only raised the dead. The game was already flawed,
and since I didn't gain information with this, I decided to continue:
Put blindfold -> Apply bell -> Remove blindfold -> read +oD -> Put
blindfold.
The misterious force was annoying as usual, but at least Rodney didn't
appear before the planes.

The planes:
This run I got the most annoying water plane ever (it was also kind of
epic). I couldn't find the portal, and Rodney appeared 3 times. The
1st time was just to say hi. The 2nd time was to cast double trouble
and steal the amulet. I managed to kill both quickly, but now I had
lost the amulet. Fortunately, the 3rd time Rodney appeared he
teleported to the amulet to pick it up and bring it back to me.
Eventually I hit the portal and entered astral plane. The correct
altar was then third.

